    {
      "bbox": [
        211,
        1672,
        1745,
        2433
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "It was the intention of the city, in seeking the estab-\nlishment of this department, to center within it control over all\nreal estate matters except where separate procedures have been\nestablished for specific reasons. For example, the Departments\nof Marine and Aviation and Parks have such separate procedures,\nand will continue to exercise their authority in this field over\nproperty under their jurisdiction. Similarly, the Authorities,\nsuch as Housing, Transit and Triborough Bridge and Tunnel remain\nundisturbed.",
